  "text": "It's $4.58, the patient is in the chair, and the GP swears they sent the X-ray. Where the hell is it? Spoiler, it's buried in someone's inbox, in a fax tray, or on page 3 of an email chain from June. Now, meet tooth referral. Here's how it works. Every incoming referral, from every office, lands in one list you can trust. Open the patient, and the X-rays are right there, shared with both offices. The insurance card is, too, front and back. Is something missing? Message the GP inside the case. Tag them, and when they answer, it's saved with the patient. Then update the status, and the referring office sees it instantly. No more callbacks or any update? Emails. Every office you work with stays connected. That's not just software. It's a referral network that works. So, next time it's $4.58, you'll know exactly where that X-ray is. Calm, collected, and connected. Want that calm for your office? Check out tooth referral, and bring every referring office into one place.",
